      "detail": {
        "summary": "In Mark 13:2, Jesus is portrayed as telling a disciple that the Temple's great buildings will be thrown down so completely that no stone remains upon another. Later readers compare this wording with the Roman destruction of Jerusalem and the Second Temple in 70 CE. MFTL treats the wording as textual attestation and the text–event connection as an interpretive historical comparison; it does not infer supernatural fulfillment from the historical event alone.",
